

⚡ What CrashAnalyzer Is

CrashAnalyzer detects field collapse, identifies the failure type, and generates a crash signature for logs, visualization, and debugging.

It is the engine’s post‑mortem intelligence system.

It tells you:

what failed

why it failed

how it failed

where it failed

what the failure looked like in field‑space

This is essential for warp‑field physics, where failures are often sudden, nonlinear, and catastrophic.

⚡ The Three Core Responsibilities

CrashAnalyzer performs three major tasks, each one critical.

🜁 1. Detect Failure — “Did something break?”

It scans the StateLattice for:

warp‑field collapse

gravity shear spikes

stress overload

charge runaway

metric discontinuities

exotic‑regime instability

If any threshold is exceeded, it flags a failure.

This is the alarm bell.

🜂 2. Classify Failure — “What type of failure is it?”

Once a failure is detected, CrashAnalyzer determines the category:

field_collapse

shear_overload

metric_break

charge_runaway

grav_spike_failure

This is the diagnosis step.

It tells you the nature of the failure.

🜃 3. Generate Signature — “What did the failure look like?”

This is the most powerful part.

CrashAnalyzer produces a crash signature, which is a structured record of:

field values at the moment of collapse

spatial pattern of the failure

regime at time of failure

safety envelope violations

time‑to‑collapse

dominant field interactions

lattice snapshot

This signature is used by:

visualization layer

logs

replay tools

debugging

research

It’s the black‑box recording of the event.

⚡ Why CrashAnalyzer Matters

Without it:

you wouldn’t know why an organism failed

you couldn’t debug warp‑field behavior

you couldn’t tune safety envelopes

you couldn’t refine regime thresholds

you couldn’t evolve the engine intelligently

CrashAnalyzer is what turns Emphemsa from a “simulation toy” into a scientific instrument.

It gives you post‑event clarity in a domain where failures are fast, nonlinear, and catastrophic.

⚡ How CrashAnalyzer Fits Into the Engine Flow

FieldDynamicsEngine → evolves fields
RegimeOrchestrator  → determines mode
PermissionLayer     → enforces limits
CrashAnalyzer       → detects and explains failure

It is the final line of analysis.



